{
 "summary": "Between about 00:12:47Z and 00:14:46Z, checkout requests failed fast with 502s that trace back to inventory POST /reserve returning 500. During the same window inventory logged 'connection reset by peer', so the likely cause is inventory losing connections to a dependency the snapshot does not identify. Errors had stopped by the end of the window (last 5xx ratio 0 on all services), and no deployment records were found.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory POST /reserve returned 500s because its connections were reset ('connection reset by peer', 44 times). Orders turned these into 502s and the gateway turned them into checkout 502s. The peer that reset the connections, probably an inventory backend dependency, is not visible in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-a54c7699226e",
   "ev-c30708431859",
   "ev-a57a947e1357",
   "ev-01577e4a4821",
   "ev-da66dff6a849"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders and gateway pass inventory's failure straight to the client: every sampled error trace and every failure log shows the same chain, inventory 500 to orders 502 to gateway 502, with no evidence of retry or fallback.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a54c7699226e",
    "ev-a57a947e1357",
    "ev-01577e4a4821"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "The failures were intermittent and short-lived. The error ratio peaked at 33.8% on inventory and orders and 22.1% on gateway, but averaged 5.6–8.5% and ended at 0.",
